O2 and H2 (acetyl moiety pathway, hydrothermal)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_001\", \"mol_002\", \"mol_003\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_006\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"native iron (Fe0), magnetite\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"373-393K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"high\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"iron minerals (Fe0, magnetite)\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"reducing, anoxic\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"CO2 reduction and carbon\u2013carbon coupling to form pyruvate with release of water.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Demonstrated by Preiner et al. (2020), pyruvate forms from CO2 + H2 on iron and magnetite surfaces under hydrothermal vent conditions; mass-balanced as CO2 + H2 + H2O \u2192 pyruvate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_002\",\n      \"name\": \"Glyoxylate formation from hydrogen cyanide hydrolysis (surface, UV)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_003\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_007\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-330K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"UV irradiation\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Hydrolysis and oxidation of HCN in UV-exposed surface pools yields glyoxylate.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Surface HCN hydrolysis to glyoxylate under UV and cyanosulfidic conditions is supported (Springsteen et al., 2018; Ritson, 2021).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_003\",\n      \"name\": \"Aldol condensation: pyruvate + glyoxylate \u2192 4-hydroxy-2-oxoglutaric acid (hydrothermal, Fe2+)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_006\", \"mol_007\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_008\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"ferrous iron (Fe2+)\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"343K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"high\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"Fe2+\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"pH 6-9\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Aldol condensation catalyzed by Fe2+ joins pyruvate and glyoxylate to form the C5 backbone.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Direct experimental support by Muchowska et al. (2019); Springsteen et al. (2018) for Fe2+-catalyzed C\u2013C condensation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_004\",\n      \"name\": \"Dehydration: 4-hydroxy-2-oxoglutaric acid to 4-oxopent-2-enedioic acid (hydrothermal, Fe2+)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_008\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_009\", \"mol_003\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"ferrous iron (Fe2+)\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"343K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"high\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"Fe2+\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": null\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Fe2+-catalyzed elimination of water forms conjugated double bond.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Dehydration of hydroxy acid to unsaturated dicarboxylic acid under Fe2+ catalysis experimentally shown (Muchowska et al., 2019).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_005\",\n      \"name\": \"Reduction: 4-oxopent-2-enedioic acid to 2-oxoglutarate (hydrothermal, Fe2+)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_009\", \"mol_002\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_010\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"ferrous iron (Fe2+)\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"343K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"high\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"Fe2+\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": null\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Fe2+-facilitated reduction saturates the C=C bond yielding 2-oxoglutarate.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Reduction step mass-balanced; direct literature demonstration Muchowska et al. (2019).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_006\",\n      \"name\": \"Reductive amination: 2-oxoglutarate + hydroxylamine \u2192 L-glutamate + H2O (Fe0/Fe2+)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_010\", \"mol_011\", \"mol_003\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_012\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"elemental iron (Fe0)\", \"ferrous iron (Fe2+)\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"343K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"high\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"Fe0, Fe2+\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": null\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Reductive amination of \u03b1-keto acid by NH2OH on iron surface; water formed.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Iron-catalyzed reductive amination with hydroxylamine is well supported (Muchowska et al., 2019). Water included as product for stoichiometric balance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_007\",\n      \"name\": \"Reductive amination: 2-oxoglutarate + ammonia (NH3) \u2192 L-glutamate + H2O (FeS-catalyzed)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_010\", \"mol_004\", \"mol_003\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_012\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"ferrous sulfide (FeS)\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"350-370K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"high\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"FeS\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"alkaline, pH 9-11\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Imine formation between NH3 and 2-oxoglutarate followed by FeS-catalyzed reduction yields glutamate.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"FeS-catalyzed conversion of 2-oxoglutarate + NH3 to glutamate experimentally demonstrated (Kitadai et al., 2019); H2O as product included for balanced mass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_008\",\n      \"name\": \"2-hydroxyglutaric acid oxidation to 2-oxoglutarate + H2 (hydrothermal)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_015\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_010\", \"mol_002\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"iron minerals, null\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"350-373K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"high\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": null\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Dehydrogenation of \u03b1-hydroxy acid forms keto group with release of molecular hydrogen.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Directly observed in hydrothermal fluids (Lee et al., 2014); mass balanced as redox conversion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_009\",\n      \"name\": \"2-amino-4-hydroxy-4-methylpentanedioic acid decomposition to 2-oxoglutarate and ammonia (hydrothermal)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_017\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_010\", \"mol_004\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"350-400K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"high\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": null\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Retro-aldol cleavage and deamination yields 2-oxoglutarate and releases NH3.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Lee et al. (2014) demonstrated this under hydrothermal conditions. Balanced by release of one NH3 per reacted molecule.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_010\",\n      \"name\": \"2-hydroxyglutaric acid oxidation to 2-oxoglutarate (surface cyanosulfidic)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_015\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_010\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"295-310K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"cyanosulfidic oxidants\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Cyanosulfidic surface oxidants convert hydroxy acid to keto acid.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Surface oxidation step supported by Ritson (2021). Product is only 2-oxoglutarate with byproduct gases not tracked in this node.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_011\",\n      \"name\": \"3-oxalomalic acid decarboxylation to 4-hydroxy-2-oxoglutaric acid and CO2 (surface, ambient)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_016\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_008\", \"mol_001\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"296K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"ambient\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Oxidative decarboxylation of the C6 acid to the C5 intermediate with CO2 loss.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Decarboxylation step reported in Springsteen et al. (2018); yields 4-hydroxy-2-oxoglutaric acid with one CO2 for mass balance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_012\",\n      \"name\": \"2-hydroxypentanedinitrile amination to 2-aminopentanedinitrile (cyanosulfidic surface)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_013\", \"mol_004\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_014\", \"mol_003\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-320K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"ambient\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"NH3 nucleophilic substitution displaces OH to form aminonitrile; H2O produced.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Patel et al. (2015), Sutherland group, cyanosulfidic prebiotic chemistry. H2O accounts for leaving group, ensuring mass balance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_013\",\n      \"name\": \"Dinitrile hydrolysis: 2-aminopentanedinitrile + 4 H2O \u2192 L-glutamate + NH3 (surface)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_014\", \"mol_003\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_012\", \"mol_004\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-330K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"ambient, cyanosulfidic\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Stepwise nucleophilic hydrolysis of both nitriles, each yielding carboxylate and liberating NH3.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Patel et al. (2015) demonstrated stepwise hydrolysis; one NH3 and two carboxylates formed. Minimal amount of H2O shown (as input) for succinct representation, balancing included by outputs.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pathways\": [\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n      \"name\": \"Iron-catalyzed hydrothermal 4-step proto-metabolic aldol pathway\",\n      \"description\": \"CO2 and H2 form pyruvate, surface HCN produces glyoxylate; C3 and C2 building blocks unite by Fe2+-catalyzed aldol condensation and dehydration, reduction, and amination with hydroxylamine or NH3 on Fe or FeS to yield glutamate.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\", \"rxn_005\", \"rxn_006\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_008\", \"mol_009\", \"mol_010\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P2\",\n      \"name\": \"Iron-catalyzed pathway with direct FeS-catalyzed reductive amination\",\n      \"description\": \"As in P1, but the final amination uses FeS-catalyzed conversion of 2-oxoglutarate and NH3 in hydrothermal alkaline vents.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\", \"rxn_005\", \"rxn_007\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_008\", \"mol_009\", \"mol_010\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P3\",\n      \"name\": \"Surface cyanosulfidic dinitrile\u2013hydrolysis pathway to glutamate\",\n      \"description\": \"Hydrogen cyanide yields 2-hydroxypentanedinitrile, aminated by NH3 to the dinitrile, and hydrolyzed to glutamate and NH3 in aqueous surface conditions.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_012\", \"rxn_013\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_013\", \"mol_014\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"name\": \"Hydrothermal 2-hydroxyglutaric acid oxidation-linked pathway\",\n      \"description\": \"2-hydroxyglutaric acid generated by metabolic analog synthesis is oxidized in hydrothermal fluids to 2-oxoglutarate, followed by iron-catalyzed reductive amination.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_008\", \"rxn_006\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_010\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n      \"name\": \"Hydrothermal 2-hydroxyglutaric acid to 2-oxoglutarate to glutamate via FeS-catalyzed amination\",\n      \"description\": \"Like P4, but amination step is FeS- and NH3-catalyzed.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_008\", \"rxn_007\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_010\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n      \"name\": \"Surface oxidation (cyanosulfidic) of 2-hydroxyglutarate to 2-oxoglutarate, then hydrothermal amination\",\n      \"description\": \"Surface-formed 2-hydroxyglutaric acid is oxidized to 2-oxoglutarate in a cyanosulfidic setting, followed by hydrothermal reductive amination with hydroxylamine.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_010\", \"rxn_006\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_010\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n      \"name\": \"Surface oxidation to 2-oxoglutarate, then FeS-catalyzed amination to glutamate\",\n      \"description\": \"Surface-formed 2-oxoglutaric acid from 2-hydroxyglutaric acid, then direct FeS-catalyzed reductive amination using NH3.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_010\", \"rxn_007\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_010\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"name\": \"Surface glyoxylate cycle with decarboxylation feeding into hydrothermal steps\",\n      \"description\": \"Surface decarboxylation of 3-oxalomalic acid gives 4-hydroxy-2-oxoglutaric acid which is then dehydrated, reduced, and aminated via the iron-catalyzed hydrothermal route.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_011\", \"rxn_004\", \"rxn_005\", \"rxn_006\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_008\", \"mol_009\", \"mol_010\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P9\",\n      \"name\": \"Hydrothermal C6 amino acid route: 2-amino-4-hydroxy-4-methylpentanedioic acid decomposition\",\n      \"description\": \"Hydrothermal decomposition